      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 7\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_{1}:=2R_{1}$ on $A?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation $R_{1}:=2R_{1}$ means that we need to multiply the first row of the matrix by $2.$\n\nMultiplying the $1$st row by $2$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A &= \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 7\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{1}:=2R_{1} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2\\cdot 1 & 2\\cdot 2 & 2\\cdot 3 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 7\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 7\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
