      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_{2}:=R_{2}+(-3)\\cdot R_{1}$ on $B?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation $R_{2}:=R_{2}+(-3)\\cdot R_{1}$ means that we need to add $-3$ times the first row to the second row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B &= \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{2}:=R_{2}+(-3)\\cdot R_{1} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3+(-3)(1) & -4+(-3)(-1) & 4+(-3)(2)\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
